# text = Am I rightly informed ," he says -- not exactly through his nose , but as if he'd got a stoppage in it , very high up --" that you're a-going to the Walley of Eden ?" " I heard some talk on it ," I told him . " Oh !" says he , " if you should ever happen to go to bed there -- you MAY , you know ," he says , " in course of time as civilisation progresses -- don't forget to take a axe with you ." I looks at him tolerable hard . " Fleas ?" says I . " And more ," says he . " Wampires ?" says I . " And more ," says he . " Musquitoes , perhaps ?" says I . " And more ," says he . "
